## Plans

Use direct implementation for one clear, reversible, low-risk local diff with
one bounded acceptance path. Direct work creates no tracked plan, reviewer, or
automatic commit. Use a canonical plan for explicit planning, multi-commit or
cross-repository work, scheduling, cold handoff, unresolved decisions,
cross-subsystem/public-contract changes, security-sensitive or destructive
work, or an external effect. Never create a placeholder plan to unlock review.

<constraint>
The ownership topology is exactly three skills. `plan-workspace` maintains the
workspace. Main-context `plan-manager` owns classify → draft/review/one repair →
start → implement/delegate → observed acceptance → finish/archive, plus list,
show, lifecycle, and guarded GitHub issue publication. Internal `plan-reviewer`
returns read-only `PlanReviewV1` evidence from one immutable bundle. Only the
reviewer has a wrapper; main invokes `plan-manager` directly.
</constraint>

<constraint>
A current canonical plan has one unfenced
`Plan-run: <compact JCS PlanRunV1>` line. Schemas 1–6 are historical
validation/quarantine formats only and never current authority. List/audit scan
frontmatter first; malformed legacy evidence is target-locally quarantined and
never blocks an unrelated goal.
</constraint>

`PlanRunV1` binds `goal_id`, `run_id`, `repository_id`, normalized `plan_path`,
canonical `requested_effects`, `risk`, canonical plan/source hashes, independent
`draft_review` and `completion_review` phases, execution/implementation commit
identities, final acceptance hashes, and at most one typed blocker. The run
identity is `repository_id + plan_path + run_id`; cross-repository child runs
share `goal_id`.

Each review phase uses
`not_required|not_started|reserved|retryable|repairing|passed|degraded|blocked|cancelled`
and at most two invocations. Reserve and persist the exact input hash before a
fresh launch; a lost result consumes the permit, stale results are discarded,
and cold `reserved` blocks without redispatch. Local draft review may degrade
only after the second transport failure. Sensitive/external work never degrades.
Ordinary local work has no completion review; sensitive, destructive,
public-contract, security, or external work reviews the exact implementation
commit/diff with at most one blocker-fix re-review.

Every mutation runs under an exclusive per-plan lock with exact preimage,
closed reduction, sibling write+fsync, atomic rename, and read-back. Checkpoint
commits also lock the repository and verify HEAD, index, and owned paths. Direct
work makes no automatic commit; plan-only makes one; ordinary canonical work
makes start/final checkpoints; sensitive/external work makes
start/implementation/archive checkpoints. Never auto-push.

Every plan Steps row has `Effect` exactly
`local|probe|production_access|publish|push|release|deploy`. Persisted effects
record intent only. Each non-local action requires live
`ExternalAuthorityV1 {scopes,mode,targets,source_sha256}` derived from the exact
current-user message, matching exact scope/mode/target at the boundary. Probe is
read-only and non-transitive; cold recovery requires new authority.

For `--issues` / `publish <slug> as an issue`, require live `publish` authority,
an existing canonical plan, successful `gh auth status`, a GitHub remote, and
`gh repo view --json visibility`. Warn and obtain explicit confirmation before
publishing sensitive plan content to a public repository. Failure creates no
issue or plan write.

The complete closed frontmatter/status matrix, PlanRunV1 schema, review outputs,
transaction rules, effects contract, and legacy policy live in
`docs/plans/AGENTS.md`; `docs/plans/CLAUDE.md` is exactly `@AGENTS.md`.

## Tool-agnostic rules

- Install locked dependencies before running project validators.
- Run focused checks while editing and the project-required final gate once.
- Skill bodies stay within the agentskills.io limit; prefer the 80–310 line
  recurring-context range.
- Keep manifest versions synchronized across both plugin manifests and both
  marketplace catalogs.
- Never loosen a validator floor to pass; fix the source.
